    "content": "The yellow fever vaccine (e.g., YF-VAX) is a highly effective, single-dose injection providing lifelong immunity against the virus for travelers aged 9 months or older visiting high-risk areas in Africa and South America. It must be administered at least 10 days before travel at designated, certified centers.Key Information:Recommendation: Recommended for travelers to endemic areas in Africa/South America and required for entry into specific countries.Effectiveness & Schedule: A single dose provides 95% immunity within one week, generally lasting for life without needing a booster.Side Effects: Generally mild, including headaches, muscle aches, and low-grade fevers. Rare but severe reactions can include allergic reactions or serious nervous system/organ issues.Contraindications: Individuals over 60, pregnant/breastfeeding women, or those with compromised immune systems should consult a doctor due to higher risks.Cost: Costs vary by provider and insurance, usually ranging from $150 to over $300 for the vaccine and administration fee.Vaccination Certificate:An International Certificate of Vaccination or Prophylaxis (ICVP) is issued upon vaccination and is required for entry into many countries, validating that the vaccine was given at an authorized center.Alternatives:If a medical exemption is needed, travellers should consult their physician. The yellow fever vaccine (e.g., YF-VAX) is a highly effective, single-dose injection providing lifelong immunity against the virus for travelers aged 9 months or older visiting high-risk areas in Africa and South America. It must be administered at least 10 days before travel at designated, certified centers. designated, certified centers Key Information: Recommendation: Recommended for travelers to endemic areas in Africa/South America and required for entry into specific countries. Effectiveness & Schedule: A single dose provides 95% immunity within one week, generally lasting for life without needing a booster